:: day2_hub [nobr]
<!--
  PLACEHOLDER   pipeline test only, AND the current end of the
  public build's content (female route).
  As of v0.2, this route deliberately does NOT show
  <<endOfContentNotice>> - Day 1 is real, playable content now, so
  the female route flows straight through it without an "end of
  public build" interruption; it just quietly runs out of content
  here until Day 2 is written. (The futa route still shows the
  notice, at day1_hub_futa.tw, since its Day 1 doesn't exist yet.)
  Replace with real Day 2 ("Body") content and its own day2fInit
  flag block (mirroring day1f-init.tw) when written.
-->
<div class="day-transition">
  <h2><<print formatDayNumber($dayNumber)>>   Body</h2>
  <p>(Day 2 content not yet written. Days -2 through Day 1 are
  fully playable end to end on the female route   the Rite, the
  first day of recovery in the Moonspire Tower, and everything
  before it.)</p>
  <p><<print $mcName>>, <<print $mcTitle>>. Height <<print $mcHeight>>,
  bust <<print $mcBust>>. Stress: <<print $stress>> | Energy: <<print $energy>></p>
</div>
